{#-
  Lesson-plan delivery audit (WeasyPrint).

  Answers "which call missed which key, and why" for the frozen cohort, at the
  grain a researcher can act on: one row per core step, because one core step is
  exactly one C1 call.

  Structure:
    - Institution band, title, and what the pack is for.
    - Cohort summary: each manipulation key against each lesson (multi-lesson only).
    - Per lesson: the call grid, then one card per call that lost a key, giving
      the mechanism counted from the plan and — where the key was student_tasks —
      the task-shaped lines in her note with a decision box each.

  Every value is plain text through Jinja autoescaping. Nothing here is markdown
  and nothing is emitted with `safe`: the note lines are the teacher's verbatim
  text and are shown as written, unrendered, so a reader compares them with the
  page rather than with a formatting of them.
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Lesson-plan delivery audit</title>
  <style>{{ stylesheet | safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="packet-code-anchor">{{ pack_code }}</div>

  <p class="institution">{{ institution_name }}</p>
  <p class="study-title">{{ study_title }}</p>
  <hr class="band-rule">

  <h1 class="doc-title">Lesson-plan delivery audit</h1>
  <p class="eyebrow">What C1 actually received, call by call</p>

  <p class="body">
    C1 is the condition that adds the lesson plan's design to C0's curriculum
    objective. One core step is one independent model call, so a key that the plan
    had nothing for is simply absent from that call's prompt — and once rendered,
    absent and withheld look the same. This pack reports, per call, which of the
    six keys arrived and what in the plan explains each miss.
  </p>
  <p class="legend">&#10003; = the key reached this call &#183; &#8212; = it did not</p>

{% if summary %}
  <h2 class="heading">The manipulation, per lesson</h2>
  <table class="summary-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Key C1 adds over C0</th>
      {% for lesson in summary.lessons %}
      <th>{{ lesson }}</th>
      {% endfor %}
      <th>Cohort</th>
    </tr>
    {% for row in summary.rows %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.short }}</td>
      {% for cell in row.cells %}
      <td class="count">{{ cell }}</td>
      {% endfor %}
      <td class="total">{{ row.cohort }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
{% endif %}

{% for lesson in lessons %}
  <div class="{{ 'page-break' if not loop.first or summary else '' }}">
    <h2 class="lesson-head">{{ lesson.lesson }} &#183; {{ lesson.topic }}</h2>
    <p class="lesson-meta">
      {{ lesson.subtopic }}{% if lesson.subtopic %} &#183; {% endif %}
      {{ lesson.term }}, week {{ lesson.week }} &#183;
      {{ lesson.calls }} core step{{ '' if lesson.calls == 1 else 's' }} = {{ lesson.calls }} C1
      call{{ '' if lesson.calls == 1 else 's' }} &#183;
      {{ lesson.evaluation_steps }} evaluation step{{ '' if lesson.evaluation_steps == 1 else 's' }}
    </p>

    <table class="calls-table">
      <tr>
        <th>Call</th>
        <th>Step</th>
        {% for head in key_heads %}
        <th class="key-head">{{ head }}</th>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
      {% for step in lesson.steps %}
      <tr>
        <td class="mark">{{ step.position }}</td>
        <td class="call-step">{{ step.step_id }}</td>
        {% for mark in step.marks %}
        <td class="mark{{ ' absent' if not mark.present else '' }}">
          {{ '&#10003;' | safe if mark.present else '&#8212;' | safe }}
        </td>
        {% endfor %}
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>

    {% for step in lesson.steps if step.missing %}
    <div class="miss-card keep-together">
      <h3>Call {{ step.position }} &#183; {{ step.step_id }}{% if step.title %} &#8212; {{ step.title }}{% endif %}</h3>
      <p class="miss-objective">{{ step.objective_id }}: {{ step.objective_text }}</p>
      <ul class="miss-list">
        {% for miss in step.missing %}
        <li><span class="miss-key">{{ miss.short }}</span> did not arrive &#8212; {{ miss.reason }}.</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>

      {% if step.tasks %}
      <div class="tasks">
        <p class="tasks-lead">
          Task-shaped lines in her note for this step, and what the note does next.
          Decide each against the source page: only the page says whether she set it.
        </p>
        {% for task in step.tasks %}
        <div class="task">
          <p class="task-line">{{ task.line }}</p>
          {% if task.followed_by %}
          <p class="task-context">followed by &#8220;{{ task.followed_by }}&#8221; &#8212; {{ task.meaning }}</p>
          {% endif %}
          <p class="task-decide">
            <span class="choice"><span class="marker marker-square"></span>work she set</span>
            <span class="choice"><span class="marker marker-square"></span>work she demonstrated</span>
            <span class="choice"><span class="marker marker-square"></span>not a task</span>
          </p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
{% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
